<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cakraningrat IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1753</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cakraningrat IV was a prince of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madura">Madura</a> who ruled from the 1720s. Seeking independence from Mataram, he took part in the wars of the 1740s, first siding with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> and then turning against it when it refused him eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. He was defeated, captured and in 1745 exiled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-of-good-hope">Cape of Good Hope</a>, where he died.</p></div>
